{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Wherefore it is said in the Book of the Wars of YHWH.</b> Concerning this encampment and the miracles that were performed in it. <b>In the Book of the Wars of YHWH</b> — this was a book unto itself, and the wars of YHWH on behalf of those who fear Him were recorded there. And it is possible that it was from the days of Abraham, for many books have been lost to us in exile and are not found among us, such as the words of Nathan and Iddo, and the chronicles of the kings of Israel, and the songs and proverbs of Solomon. Thus explained the Rav, Rabbi Abraham, of blessed memory."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:35.869747535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}